' WELCOME.SPK - the Welcome Wagon, for the central host (STARTHERE). Every
' machine runs a Chat service (port 6667), and the Chat program connects to
' its own machine's, in #general, out of the box: so somebody new who opens
' Chat finds an empty room. The Welcome Wagon looks round the network every
' half minute (NET.Machines) and waits in #general on every machine as
' StartHereBot. When somebody comes into the room (or is there already), it
' says hello, once, and tells them what this machine serves (the same list
' as SimHost's front page).
'
' It also links the rooms into one: everybody in #general on any machine
' is in #general on every machine where somebody is. Each person gets a
' stand-in in the other rooms, a connection of the bot's own under their
' name, which says what they say there; so "<newbie> hi all" reads the same
' everywhere, and the list of who's here is everybody on the network. A
' room nobody is in gets no stand-ins. In a room:
'   sites    the sites here, one a line
'   unlink   this room stays to itself (C:\WELCOME\UNLINK.TXT); link undoes it
'   bye      it leaves that machine's room, for good (C:\WELCOME\OPTOUT.TXT)
' A name somebody in another room already has can't be passed through (the
' Chat service won't have two): that person is told, once, and isn't heard
' in that room until they change their name.
' Settings, in C:\WELCOME\WELCOME.INI:
'   channel=#general    the room to wait in
'   every=30            seconds between looks round the network
' Whom it has greeted is in C:\WELCOME\SEEN.TXT (machine|nick).
'
' One Connect a tick, the last thing in it, inside a TRY: a failed wait
' spoils the rest of its handler (see SIM95-NOTES.md).
'
' The Chat service runs each line it gets as a task of its own, and a long
' one can be overtaken by the next: lines sent together arrive shuffled, and
' a JOIN can come before the NICK sent ahead of it. So the bot joins only
' once its name is taken, says one line a tick, and greets somebody a moment
' after they come in, by the name they have by then.

CONST HOME = "C:\WELCOME"
CONST BOTNICK = "StartHereBot"
CONST RETRY = 300000              ' a machine with no Chat service is tried again after this (ms)
CONST RETRYSOON = 10000           ' ...one whose Chat service was there (it may have crashed: see SIM95-NOTES.md)
CONST QUIET = 20000               ' the list of sites at most this often in one room (ms)
CONST MOST = 200                  ' lines kept in the window
CONST SETTLE = 1500               ' greet this long after somebody comes in (ms)
CONST MOSTLINKS = 300             ' stand-ins at most, all told

VAR EOL AS String
VAR win AS GUI_Window
VAR journal AS GUI_ListBox
VAR clock AS GUI_Timer
VAR sock AS NET_Socket
VAR noted AS Array OF String      ' the window's lines

VAR channel AS String
VAR every AS Integer              ' seconds
VAR here AS String                ' this machine as people type it: starthere
VAR lookedAt AS Integer           ' when it last looked round (0: never)
VAR looking AS Bool
VAR connecting AS Bool
VAR connectAt AS Integer
VAR seen AS Array OF String       ' MACHINE|nick: greeted already
VAR greeted AS Integer            ' since it started

' The rooms, one a machine (this one's too, as localhost).
VAR rName AS Array OF String      ' A3F9C2E1.DIALUP.ZONE
VAR rAddr AS Array OF String
VAR rState AS Array OF String     ' new, open, off (no answer), gone (closed), left (said bye)
VAR rSince AS Array OF Integer
VAR rNick AS Array OF String      ' the name it has there
VAR rListed AS Array OF Integer   ' when it last listed the sites there

VAR rLinked AS Array OF Bool      ' FALSE when somebody there said unlink
VAR rTold AS Array OF Bool        ' told (since it started) that the room is linked
VAR rWasOpen AS Array OF Bool     ' it has been in the room before

' The open connections, by tag: a room's name for the bot's own, "#" and a
' number for a stand-in.
VAR cName AS Array OF String
VAR cConn AS Array OF NET_Connection

' Waiting a moment (for their NICK to catch up): room, nick, since when, and
' whether to say hello.
VAR gRoom AS Array OF String
VAR gNick AS Array OF String
VAR gAt AS Array OF Integer
VAR gHello AS Array OF Bool

' Recent renames (room, old, new, when): a NICK can reach the bot before the
' JOIN it followed, and the JOIN still has the old name.
VAR nRoom AS Array OF String
VAR nOld AS Array OF String
VAR nNew AS Array OF String
VAR nAt AS Array OF Integer

' Lines to send, one a tick for each connection: tag, then the line.
VAR oRoom AS Array OF String
VAR oText AS Array OF String
VAR sending AS Bool
VAR sendingAt AS Integer

' The people in the rooms (not the bot, not stand-ins).
VAR hId AS Array OF Integer
VAR hRoom AS Array OF String
VAR hNick AS Array OF String
VAR nextId AS Integer

' Stand-ins: whose (a person's id), in which room, under what name, and how
' far along: wait (to connect), naming (NICK sent), in (JOINed), dead (QUIT sent).
VAR uId AS Array OF Integer
VAR uWho AS Array OF Integer
VAR uRoom AS Array OF String
VAR uNick AS Array OF String
VAR uState AS Array OF String
VAR clashed AS Array OF String    ' "id|room": the name is taken there
VAR linker AS GUI_Timer
VAR pConnecting AS Bool
VAR pConnectAt AS Integer

SUB Main ()
    VAR line AS String
    EOL = Chr(10)
    IF NOT FS.Exists(HOME) THEN FS.MakeDir(HOME)
    channel = "#general"
    every = 30
    FOR EACH line IN ReadOr(HOME + "\WELCOME.INI", "").Lines()
        IF line.StartsWith("channel=") THEN channel = line.Substring(8, line.Length - 8).Trim().Lower()
        IF line.StartsWith("every=") THEN every = MATH.Max(1, Int(Val(line.Substring(6, line.Length - 6))))
    NEXT
    IF NOT channel.StartsWith("#") THEN channel = "#" + channel
    here = NET.HostName.Split(".")[0].Lower()
    FOR EACH line IN ReadOr(HOME + "\SEEN.TXT", "").Lines()
        IF line <> "" THEN seen.Add(line)
    NEXT

    win = GUI_Window.New("Welcome Wagon", 480, 260)
    win.Icon = "chat"
    win.onClose = Win_OnClose
    journal = GUI_ListBox.New(win)
    journal.SetBounds(6, 6, 468, 226)
    sock = NET_Socket.New()
    sock.onMessage = Room_OnMessage
    sock.onClose = Room_OnClose
    ' this machine's own room too: it is where people are sent to meet
    AddRoom(NET.HostName.Upper(), "localhost")
    clock = GUI_Timer.New(win)
    clock.Interval = 500
    clock.onTick = Clock_OnTick
    clock.Start()
    ' stand-ins connect on a clock of their own, quicker
    linker = GUI_Timer.New(win)
    linker.Interval = 150
    linker.onTick = Linker_OnTick
    linker.Start()
    Note("Greeting people in " + channel + " on every machine, for http://" + here + "/, and linking the rooms")
    Status()
    win.Show()
END SUB

SUB Win_OnClose ()
    SYS.Exit(0)
END SUB

FUNCTION ReadOr (path AS String, fallback AS String) AS String
    IF FS.Exists(path) THEN RETURN FS.Read(path)
    RETURN fallback
END FUNCTION

SUB Note (text AS String)
    noted.Add(TIME.Clock + "  " + text)
    IF noted.Count > MOST THEN noted.RemoveAt(0)
    journal.Items = noted
    journal.ScrollToEnd()
END SUB

SUB Status ()
    VAR n AS Integer
    VAR s AS String
    FOR EACH s IN rState
        IF s = "open" THEN n = n + 1
    NEXT
    win.Status = Str(n) + " room" + Plural(n) + " open  -  " + Str(hId.Count) + " " + People(hId.Count) + " in them  -  " + Str(uState.Count) + " stand-in" + Plural(uState.Count) + "  -  " + Str(greeted) + " greeted since it started"
END SUB

FUNCTION Plural (n AS Integer) AS String
    IF n = 1 THEN RETURN ""
    RETURN "s"
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION People (n AS Integer) AS String
    IF n = 1 THEN RETURN "person"
    RETURN "people"
END FUNCTION

' ================================================================ the rooms

SUB AddRoom (name AS String, addr AS String)
    rName.Add(name)
    rAddr.Add(addr)
    rState.Add("new")
    rSince.Add(SYS.Ticks)
    rNick.Add(BOTNICK)
    rListed.Add(0)
    rLinked.Add(NOT InFile(HOME + "\UNLINK.TXT", name))
    rTold.Add(FALSE)
    rWasOpen.Add(FALSE)
    IF OptedOut(name) THEN rState[rState.Count - 1] = "left"
END SUB

SUB SetState (i AS Integer, s AS String)
    rState[i] = s
    rSince[i] = SYS.Ticks
END SUB

FUNCTION IsHub (i AS Integer) AS Bool
    RETURN rAddr[i] = "localhost"
END FUNCTION

' Said bye: by computer name, so a new address or ISP doesn't bring it back.
FUNCTION OptedOut (name AS String) AS Bool
    RETURN InFile(HOME + "\OPTOUT.TXT", name)
END FUNCTION

' Is the machine (by computer name) in the file, one name a line?
FUNCTION InFile (path AS String, name AS String) AS Bool
    VAR line AS String
    FOR EACH line IN ReadOr(path, "").Lines()
        IF line.Trim().Upper() = name.Split(".")[0].Upper() THEN RETURN TRUE
    NEXT
    RETURN FALSE
END FUNCTION

' The machine as people say it: newbie, starthere
FUNCTION Called (room AS String) AS String
    RETURN room.Split(".")[0].Lower()
END FUNCTION

' ================================================================ the clock

SUB Clock_OnTick ()
    TRY
        Tick()
    CATCH err
    END TRY
END SUB

SUB Tick ()
    VAR i AS Integer
    VAR room AS String
    VAR nick AS String
    VAR hello AS Bool
    ' somebody who came in a moment ago: hello now, by the name they have,
    ' and into the other rooms (one a tick, off the list first: ticks overlap
    ' while one waits)
    IF gRoom.Count > 0 THEN
        IF SYS.Ticks - gAt[0] >= SETTLE THEN
            room = gRoom[0]
            nick = gNick[0]
            hello = gHello[0]
            gRoom.RemoveAt(0)
            gNick.RemoveAt(0)
            gAt.RemoveAt(0)
            gHello.RemoveAt(0)
            i = rName.IndexOf(room)
            IF i >= 0 THEN
                IF rState[i] = "open" THEN
                    AddPerson(room, nick)
                    IF hello THEN Greet(i, nick)
                    Spread()
                END IF
            END IF
        END IF
    END IF
    ' a line for each connection that has one waiting
    IF NOT sending OR SYS.Ticks - sendingAt > 3000 THEN
        sending = TRUE
        sendingAt = SYS.Ticks
        SendSome()
        sending = FALSE
    END IF
    ' (a look round or a Connect waits, and ticks go on meanwhile)
    IF looking AND SYS.Ticks - lookedAt < 5000 THEN RETURN
    looking = FALSE
    IF connecting AND SYS.Ticks - connectAt < 15000 THEN RETURN
    connecting = FALSE
    IF lookedAt = 0 OR SYS.Ticks - lookedAt > every * 1000 THEN
        looking = TRUE
        lookedAt = MATH.Max(1, SYS.Ticks)
        LookRound()
        looking = FALSE
        RETURN
    END IF
    FOR i = 0 TO rName.Count - 1
        IF rState[i] = "off" AND (SYS.Ticks - rSince[i] > RETRY OR (rWasOpen[i] AND SYS.Ticks - rSince[i] > RETRYSOON)) THEN SetState(i, "new")
    NEXT
    i = rState.IndexOf("new")
    IF i >= 0 THEN OpenRoom(i)
END SUB

' Every machine that answers a ping: new ones get a room, and ones whose
' room closed (the machine went away, or its Chat service restarted) get it
' back.
SUB LookRound ()
    VAR m AS String
    VAR p AS Array OF String
    VAR i AS Integer
    FOR EACH m IN NET.Machines()
        p = m.Split(" ")
        IF p.Count < 2 THEN CONTINUE
        IF p[0].Upper() = NET.HostName.Upper() OR p[1] = NET.LocalAddress THEN CONTINUE
        i = rName.IndexOf(p[0].Upper())
        IF i < 0 THEN
            AddRoom(p[0].Upper(), p[1])
            IF rState[rState.Count - 1] = "new" THEN Note("Found " + p[0])
        ELSE
            rAddr[i] = p[1]
            IF rState[i] = "gone" THEN SetState(i, "new")
        END IF
    NEXT
    Status()
END SUB

' Into the room on machine i: the last thing in the tick.
SUB OpenRoom (i AS Integer)
    VAR conn AS NET_Connection
    SetState(i, "off")            ' until it answers
    rNick[i] = BOTNICK
    connecting = TRUE
    connectAt = SYS.Ticks
    TRY
        conn = sock.Connect(rAddr[i], 6667)
        conn.Tag = rName[i]
        SetState(i, "open")
        rWasOpen[i] = TRUE
        Forget(rName[i])
        cName.Add(rName[i])
        cConn.Add(conn)
        ' (JOIN once the name is taken: see Room_OnMessage)
        conn.Send("NICK " + BOTNICK)
        connecting = FALSE
        Status()
    CATCH err
        connecting = FALSE
    END TRY
END SUB

SUB Room_OnClose (conn AS NET_Connection)
    VAR i AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    IF conn.Tag.StartsWith("#") THEN
        ' a stand-in's connection: it has gone
        Forget(conn.Tag)
        k = uId.IndexOf(Int(Val(conn.Tag.Substring(1, conn.Tag.Length - 1))))
        IF k >= 0 THEN DropStandIn(k)
        Status()
        RETURN
    END IF
    i = rName.IndexOf(conn.Tag)
    IF i < 0 THEN RETURN
    Forget(rName[i])
    ' nobody can be heard there now, and its stand-ins are gone with it
    FOR k = hId.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF hRoom[k] = rName[i] THEN RemovePerson(k)
    NEXT
    IF rState[i] = "open" THEN
        SetState(i, "gone")
        Note("Left " + rName[i] + " (closed)")
    END IF
    Spread()
END SUB

' The Chat service's lines: MSG #chan nick text | JOIN #chan nick |
' PART #chan nick | NICK #chan old new | WHO #chan a,b,c | OK ... | ERR ...
' On the bot's own connection to a room; a stand-in's go to StandInHeard.
SUB Room_OnMessage (conn AS NET_Connection, message AS String)
    VAR i AS Integer
    VAR p AS Array OF String
    VAR who AS String
    VAR cut AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    IF conn.Tag.StartsWith("#") THEN
        StandInHeard(conn, message)
        RETURN
    END IF
    i = rName.IndexOf(conn.Tag)
    IF i < 0 THEN RETURN
    p = message.Split(" ")
    SELECT CASE p[0]
        CASE "OK"
            ' its name is taken: now into the room
            IF message.StartsWith("OK You are now ") THEN
                rNick[i] = message.Substring(15, message.Length - 15).Trim()
                conn.Send("JOIN " + channel)
            END IF
        CASE "ERR"
            ' somebody there has the name: the same with a number
            IF message.Contains("Nick in use") THEN conn.Send("NICK " + BOTNICK.Substring(0, 11) + Str(Rnd(10)))
        CASE "WHO"
            ' whoever was there before it came. (Greeted, but not on this
            ' machine: the regulars there know it, and newcomers are greeted
            ' as they come.)
            IF p.Count >= 3 AND p[1] = channel THEN
                FOR EACH who IN p[2].Split(",")
                    IF who <> "" AND NOT Ours(i, who) THEN Soon(i, who, NOT IsHub(i))
                NEXT
            END IF
        CASE "JOIN"
            IF p.Count >= 3 AND p[1] = channel AND NOT Ours(i, p[2]) THEN Soon(i, p[2], TRUE)
        CASE "PART"
            IF p.Count >= 3 AND p[1] = channel AND NOT Ours(i, p[2]) THEN Gone(i, p[2])
        CASE "NICK"
            ' NICK #chan old new
            IF p.Count >= 4 AND NOT Ours(i, p[3]) THEN Renamed(i, p[2], p[3])
        CASE "MSG"
            IF p.Count >= 4 AND p[1] = channel AND NOT Ours(i, p[2]) THEN
                cut = p[0].Length + p[1].Length + p[2].Length + 3
                Relay(i, p[2], message.Substring(cut, message.Length - cut))
                Heard(conn, i, p[2], message.Substring(cut, message.Length - cut))
            END IF
    END SELECT
END SUB

' The bot itself, or one of its stand-ins, in room i.
FUNCTION Ours (i AS Integer, nick AS String) AS Bool
    VAR k AS Integer
    IF nick.Lower() = rNick[i].Lower() THEN RETURN TRUE
    FOR k = 0 TO uId.Count - 1
        IF uRoom[k] = rName[i] AND uNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() THEN RETURN TRUE
    NEXT
    RETURN FALSE
END FUNCTION

' A line for room i, said by the bot in its turn.
SUB Say (i AS Integer, text AS String)
    Queue(rName[i], text)
END SUB

' A line for a connection (by tag), sent in its turn: a connection sends one
' a tick, so the Chat service at the other end keeps them in order.
' Chr(1) + "QUIT" or Chr(1) + "NICK name" send those instead.
SUB Queue (tag AS String, text AS String)
    oRoom.Add(tag)
    oText.Add(text)
END SUB

' The first waiting line of every connection.
SUB SendSome ()
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR done AS String
    done = ","
    k = 0
    WHILE k < oRoom.Count
        IF done.Contains("," + oRoom[k] + ",") THEN
            k = k + 1
        ELSE
            done = done + oRoom[k] + ","
            SendLine(oRoom[k], oText[k])
            oRoom.RemoveAt(k)
            oText.RemoveAt(k)
        END IF
    END WHILE
END SUB

SUB SendLine (tag AS String, text AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    k = cName.IndexOf(tag)
    IF k < 0 THEN RETURN
    TRY
        IF text.StartsWith(Chr(1)) THEN
            cConn[k].Send(text.Substring(1, text.Length - 1))
        ELSE
            cConn[k].Send("MSG " + channel + " " + text)
        END IF
    CATCH err
    END TRY
END SUB

' A room's connection is closed (or about to be replaced): no more lines for it.
SUB Forget (room AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    k = cName.IndexOf(room)
    IF k >= 0 THEN
        cName.RemoveAt(k)
        cConn.RemoveAt(k)
    END IF
    FOR k = gRoom.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF gRoom[k] = room THEN
            gRoom.RemoveAt(k)
            gNick.RemoveAt(k)
            gAt.RemoveAt(k)
            gHello.RemoveAt(k)
        END IF
    NEXT
END SUB

' Somebody in room i: greeted (if hello) and linked in a moment, when
' their NICK has caught up.
SUB Soon (i AS Integer, nick AS String, hello AS Bool)
    VAR k AS Integer
    nick = Current(rName[i], nick)
    FOR k = 0 TO gRoom.Count - 1
        IF gRoom[k] = rName[i] AND gNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() THEN RETURN
    NEXT
    gRoom.Add(rName[i])
    gNick.Add(nick)
    gAt.Add(SYS.Ticks)
    gHello.Add(hello)
END SUB

' ================================================================ what it says

' Hello, once for each person on each machine.
SUB Greet (i AS Integer, nick AS String)
    VAR key AS String
    VAR names AS Array OF String
    VAR site AS String
    VAR n AS Integer
    IF i < 0 THEN RETURN
    IF nick.Lower() = rNick[i].Lower() THEN RETURN
    key = rName[i].Split(".")[0] + "|" + nick.Lower()
    IF seen.Contains(key) THEN RETURN
    seen.Add(key)
    FS.Append(HOME + "\SEEN.TXT", key + EOL)
    greeted = greeted + 1
    FOR EACH site IN Sites()
        names.Add(site.Split("|")[0])
    NEXT
    Say(i, "Hi " + nick + ", welcome to SIM95! I'm the greeter bot from " + here.Upper() + ".")
    IF names.Count = 0 THEN
        Say(i, "Open Voyager and go to http://" + here + "/ to see what's on.")
    ELSE
        Say(i, "Open Voyager and go to http://" + here + "/ for " + Listed(names) + ".")
    END IF
    n = Elsewhere(rName[i])
    IF Linked(i) THEN
        rTold[i] = TRUE
        IF n > 0 THEN
            Say(i, "This room is linked to " + channel + " on every machine: " + Str(n) + " " + People(n) + " elsewhere on the network can talk with you here, and see what you say.")
        ELSE
            Say(i, "This room is linked to " + channel + " on every machine: whoever comes in anywhere on the network will be here too, and see what you say.")
        END IF
    ELSE
        Say(i, "Say link to talk with everybody in " + channel + " across the network (" + Str(n) + " " + People(n) + " now).")
    END IF
    IF IsHub(i) THEN
        Say(i, "Say sites for the list.")
    ELSEIF Linked(i) THEN
        Say(i, "Say sites for the list, unlink to keep this room to this machine, or bye and I'll leave it alone.")
    ELSE
        Say(i, "Say sites for the list, or bye and I'll leave this machine alone.")
    END IF
    Note("Greeted " + nick + " on " + rName[i])
    Status()
END SUB

' Somebody said something in the room: "sites", or "bye".
SUB Heard (conn AS NET_Connection, i AS Integer, nick AS String, text AS String)
    VAR t AS String
    VAR site AS String
    VAR all AS Array OF String
    VAR p AS Array OF String
    t = text.Trim().Lower()
    ' "StartHereBot: sites" too
    IF t.StartsWith(rNick[i].Lower()) THEN t = t.Substring(rNick[i].Length, t.Length - rNick[i].Length)
    t = Bare(t)
    IF t = "sites" OR t = "!sites" OR t = "help" THEN
        IF rListed[i] <> 0 AND SYS.Ticks - rListed[i] < QUIET THEN RETURN
        rListed[i] = MATH.Max(1, SYS.Ticks)
        all = Sites()
        IF all.Count = 0 THEN Say(i, "Everything is at http://" + here + "/")
        FOR EACH site IN all
            p = site.Split("|")
            Say(i, p[0] + " - " + p[1] + " - " + p[2])
        NEXT
        Note("Listed the sites for " + nick + " on " + rName[i])
    ELSEIF t = "unlink" AND IsHub(i) THEN
        Say(i, "This is where everybody meets: it stays linked.")
    ELSEIF t = "unlink" AND rLinked[i] THEN
        rLinked[i] = FALSE
        FS.Append(HOME + "\UNLINK.TXT", Called(rName[i]) + EOL)
        Say(i, "Unlinked: only people on this machine see this room now. Say link to talk with everybody again.")
        Note(nick + " unlinked " + rName[i])
        Spread()
    ELSEIF t = "link" AND NOT rLinked[i] THEN
        rLinked[i] = TRUE
        FS.Write(HOME + "\UNLINK.TXT", Without(ReadOr(HOME + "\UNLINK.TXT", ""), Called(rName[i])))
        rTold[i] = TRUE
        Say(i, "Linked: you're in " + channel + " with everybody on the network (" + Str(Elsewhere(rName[i])) + " " + People(Elsewhere(rName[i])) + " elsewhere now). Say unlink to undo it.")
        Note(nick + " linked " + rName[i])
        Spread()
    ELSEIF (t = "bye" OR t = "go away" OR t = "leave") AND NOT IsHub(i) THEN
        Say(i, "OK, I'll leave this machine alone. Find us any time at http://" + here + "/ - bye!")
        FS.Append(HOME + "\OPTOUT.TXT", Called(rName[i]) + EOL)
        SetState(i, "left")
        ' (after the goodbye, in its turn)
        Say(i, Chr(1) + "QUIT")
        Note(nick + " said bye: leaving " + rName[i] + " alone")
        Spread()
    END IF
END SUB

' The lines of text, without the one that is name (any case).
FUNCTION Without (text AS String, name AS String) AS String
    VAR out AS String
    VAR line AS String
    FOR EACH line IN text.Lines()
        IF line.Trim() <> "" AND line.Trim().Upper() <> name.Upper() THEN out = out + line.Trim() + EOL
    NEXT
    RETURN out
END FUNCTION

' ================================================================ linking the rooms

' Room i shares #general with the others: linked, and the bot is in it.
FUNCTION Linked (i AS Integer) AS Bool
    IF i < 0 THEN RETURN FALSE
    RETURN rLinked[i] AND rState[i] = "open"
END FUNCTION

' Linked, with somebody in it to read what's said.
FUNCTION Active (i AS Integer) AS Bool
    IF NOT Linked(i) THEN RETURN FALSE
    RETURN hRoom.Contains(rName[i])
END FUNCTION

' People in linked rooms other than this one.
FUNCTION Elsewhere (room AS String) AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR n AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO hId.Count - 1
        IF hRoom[k] <> room AND Linked(rName.IndexOf(hRoom[k])) THEN n = n + 1
    NEXT
    RETURN n
END FUNCTION

SUB AddPerson (room AS String, nick AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    nick = Current(room, nick)
    FOR k = 0 TO hId.Count - 1
        IF hRoom[k] = room AND hNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() THEN RETURN
    NEXT
    nextId = nextId + 1
    hId.Add(nextId)
    hRoom.Add(room)
    hNick.Add(nick)
END SUB

SUB RemovePerson (k AS Integer)
    VAR id AS Integer
    VAR m AS Integer
    id = hId[k]
    hId.RemoveAt(k)
    hRoom.RemoveAt(k)
    hNick.RemoveAt(k)
    FOR m = clashed.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF clashed[m].StartsWith(Str(id) + "|") THEN clashed.RemoveAt(m)
    NEXT
END SUB

' The name somebody has now, after any renames in the last few seconds.
FUNCTION Current (room AS String, nick AS String) AS String
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO nRoom.Count - 1
        IF nRoom[k] = room AND nOld[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() AND SYS.Ticks - nAt[k] <= 10000 THEN nick = nNew[k]
    NEXT
    RETURN nick
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION PersonAt (room AS String, nick AS String) AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO hId.Count - 1
        IF hRoom[k] = room AND hNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() THEN RETURN k
    NEXT
    RETURN -1
END FUNCTION

' Somebody left room i (PART).
SUB Gone (i AS Integer, nick AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = gRoom.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF gRoom[k] = rName[i] AND gNick[k].Lower() = nick.Lower() THEN
            gRoom.RemoveAt(k)
            gNick.RemoveAt(k)
            gAt.RemoveAt(k)
            gHello.RemoveAt(k)
        END IF
    NEXT
    k = PersonAt(rName[i], nick)
    IF k >= 0 THEN
        RemovePerson(k)
        ' their name is free here now
        FOR k = clashed.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
            IF clashed[k].EndsWith("|" + rName[i]) THEN clashed.RemoveAt(k)
        NEXT
        Spread()
    END IF
END SUB

' Somebody in room i changed their name: their stand-ins do too.
SUB Renamed (i AS Integer, old AS String, nick AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR h AS Integer
    VAR m AS Integer
    ' remembered a little while, for a JOIN still on its way
    FOR k = nAt.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF SYS.Ticks - nAt[k] > 10000 THEN
            nRoom.RemoveAt(k)
            nOld.RemoveAt(k)
            nNew.RemoveAt(k)
            nAt.RemoveAt(k)
        END IF
    NEXT
    nRoom.Add(rName[i])
    nOld.Add(old)
    nNew.Add(nick)
    nAt.Add(SYS.Ticks)
    FOR k = 0 TO gRoom.Count - 1
        IF gRoom[k] = rName[i] AND gNick[k].Lower() = old.Lower() THEN gNick[k] = nick
    NEXT
    h = PersonAt(rName[i], old)
    IF h < 0 THEN RETURN
    hNick[h] = nick
    FOR k = 0 TO uId.Count - 1
        IF uWho[k] = hId[h] AND uState[k] <> "dead" THEN
            uNick[k] = nick
            IF uState[k] <> "wait" THEN Queue("#" + Str(uId[k]), Chr(1) + "NICK " + nick)
        END IF
    NEXT
    ' a new name may be free where the old one wasn't, and the old one is
    ' free here now
    FOR m = clashed.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF clashed[m].StartsWith(Str(hId[h]) + "|") OR clashed[m].EndsWith("|" + rName[i]) THEN clashed.RemoveAt(m)
    NEXT
    Spread()
END SUB

' Somebody in room i said text: their stand-ins say it in the other rooms.
SUB Relay (i AS Integer, nick AS String, text AS String)
    VAR h AS Integer
    VAR k AS Integer
    h = PersonAt(rName[i], nick)
    IF h < 0 THEN RETURN
    FOR k = 0 TO uId.Count - 1
        IF uWho[k] = hId[h] AND uState[k] = "in" THEN Queue("#" + Str(uId[k]), text)
    NEXT
END SUB

' Every person in a linked room has a stand-in in every other linked room
' with somebody in it; nobody else has one. Called whenever that may change.
SUB Spread ()
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR h AS Integer
    VAR j AS Integer
    VAR want AS Bool
    ' stand-ins no longer wanted
    FOR k = uId.Count - 1 TO 0 STEP -1
        IF uState[k] = "dead" THEN CONTINUE
        h = hId.IndexOf(uWho[k])
        want = h >= 0
        IF want THEN want = hRoom[h] <> uRoom[k] AND Linked(rName.IndexOf(hRoom[h])) AND Active(rName.IndexOf(uRoom[k]))
        IF NOT want THEN EndStandIn(k)
    NEXT
    ' and ones that are wanted
    FOR h = 0 TO hId.Count - 1
        IF NOT Linked(rName.IndexOf(hRoom[h])) THEN CONTINUE
        FOR j = 0 TO rName.Count - 1
            IF rName[j] = hRoom[h] OR NOT Active(j) THEN CONTINUE
            IF HasStandIn(hId[h], rName[j]) OR clashed.Contains(Str(hId[h]) + "|" + rName[j]) THEN CONTINUE
            IF uId.Count >= MOSTLINKS THEN
                Note("Too many stand-ins (" + Str(MOSTLINKS) + "): not linking any more")
                RETURN
            END IF
            nextId = nextId + 1
            uId.Add(nextId)
            uWho.Add(hId[h])
            uRoom.Add(rName[j])
            uNick.Add(hNick[h])
            uState.Add("wait")
        NEXT
    NEXT
    ' a room linked with people in it who haven't been told
    FOR j = 0 TO rName.Count - 1
        IF Active(j) AND NOT rTold[j] THEN
            rTold[j] = TRUE
            Say(j, "This room is linked to " + channel + " on every machine: people elsewhere on the network see what's said here. Say unlink to keep it to this machine.")
        END IF
    NEXT
    Status()
END SUB

FUNCTION HasStandIn (who AS Integer, room AS String) AS Bool
    VAR k AS Integer
    FOR k = 0 TO uId.Count - 1
        IF uWho[k] = who AND uRoom[k] = room THEN RETURN TRUE
    NEXT
    RETURN FALSE
END FUNCTION

' Stand-in k leaves: QUIT, in its turn (it's dropped when its connection
' closes), or at once if it never connected.
SUB EndStandIn (k AS Integer)
    IF uState[k] = "wait" THEN
        DropStandIn(k)
    ELSEIF uState[k] <> "dead" THEN
        uState[k] = "dead"
        Queue("#" + Str(uId[k]), Chr(1) + "QUIT")
    END IF
END SUB

SUB DropStandIn (k AS Integer)
    uId.RemoveAt(k)
    uWho.RemoveAt(k)
    uRoom.RemoveAt(k)
    uNick.RemoveAt(k)
    uState.RemoveAt(k)
END SUB

SUB Linker_OnTick ()
    TRY
        LinkTick()
    CATCH err
    END TRY
END SUB

' One stand-in connects a tick: NICK first, JOIN once the name is taken.
SUB LinkTick ()
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR j AS Integer
    VAR id AS Integer
    VAR conn AS NET_Connection
    IF pConnecting AND SYS.Ticks - pConnectAt < 10000 THEN RETURN
    pConnecting = FALSE
    k = uState.IndexOf("wait")
    IF k < 0 THEN RETURN
    j = rName.IndexOf(uRoom[k])
    IF NOT Linked(j) THEN
        DropStandIn(k)
        RETURN
    END IF
    id = uId[k]
    uState[k] = "naming"
    pConnecting = TRUE
    pConnectAt = SYS.Ticks
    TRY
        conn = sock.Connect(rAddr[j], 6667)
        conn.Tag = "#" + Str(id)
        cName.Add(conn.Tag)
        cConn.Add(conn)
        pConnecting = FALSE
        ' (the lists may have moved while it connected)
        k = uId.IndexOf(id)
        IF k < 0 THEN
            conn.Send("QUIT")
        ELSEIF uState[k] = "dead" THEN
            conn.Send("QUIT")
        ELSE
            conn.Send("NICK " + uNick[k])
        END IF
    CATCH err
        pConnecting = FALSE
        k = uId.IndexOf(id)
        IF k >= 0 THEN DropStandIn(k)
    END TRY
END SUB

' What a stand-in's connection hears: only its own name matters.
SUB StandInHeard (conn AS NET_Connection, message AS String)
    VAR k AS Integer
    VAR h AS Integer
    VAR i AS Integer
    k = uId.IndexOf(Int(Val(conn.Tag.Substring(1, conn.Tag.Length - 1))))
    IF k < 0 THEN RETURN
    IF message.StartsWith("OK You are now ") THEN
        IF uState[k] = "naming" THEN
            uState[k] = "in"
            Queue(conn.Tag, Chr(1) + "JOIN " + channel)
            Status()
        END IF
    ELSEIF message.StartsWith("ERR Nick in use") OR message.StartsWith("ERR Bad nick") THEN
        ' the name is somebody else's there: tell its owner, once, at home
        IF uState[k] = "dead" THEN RETURN
        clashed.Add(Str(uWho[k]) + "|" + uRoom[k])
        h = hId.IndexOf(uWho[k])
        IF h >= 0 THEN
            i = rName.IndexOf(hRoom[h])
            IF i >= 0 THEN Say(i, "Somebody on " + Called(uRoom[k]) + " is already called " + hNick[h] + ", so you can't be heard there. /nick gives you another name.")
            Note(hNick[h] + "'s name is taken on " + uRoom[k])
        END IF
        EndStandIn(k)
    END IF
END SUB

' Without the bits around a word: ": sites!" -> "sites"
FUNCTION Bare (t AS String) AS String
    WHILE t.Length > 0 AND ":,; ".Contains(t.Substring(0, 1))
        t = t.Substring(1, t.Length - 1)
    END WHILE
    WHILE t.Length > 0 AND "!.? ".Contains(t.Substring(t.Length - 1, 1))
        t = t.Substring(0, t.Length - 1)
    END WHILE
    RETURN t
END FUNCTION

' "SimBook, ColdMail and AskSim"; after six, "and more".
FUNCTION Listed (names AS Array OF String) AS String
    VAR out AS String
    VAR k AS Integer
    IF names.Count = 1 THEN RETURN names[0]
    FOR k = 0 TO MATH.Min(names.Count, 6) - 1
        IF k > 0 THEN
            IF k = names.Count - 1 THEN
                out = out + " and "
            ELSE
                out = out + ", "
            END IF
        END IF
        out = out + names[k]
    NEXT
    IF names.Count > 6 THEN out = out + " and more"
    RETURN out
END FUNCTION

' The sites here, as SimHost's front page lists them: name|address|blurb.
' A folder of C:\WEB with an APP.INF (name|blurb|colour) says how it shows;
' the list below covers apps installed before they wrote one.
FUNCTION Sites () AS Array OF String
    VAR out AS Array OF String
    VAR known AS Array OF String
    VAR f AS String
    VAR k AS String
    VAR p AS Array OF String
    known = ["BOOK|BOOK.SPK|SimBook|The social network: profiles, friends, a news feed, walls, photos and pokes.", "MAIL|MAIL.SPK|ColdMail|Free webmail, with a real mail server behind it.", "ASK|ASK.SPK|AskSim|A search engine with a real crawler that goes round every machine on the network.", "GEO|GEO.SPK|GeoSimies|Free homepages for everybody: neighborhoods, hit counters, guestbooks and webrings.", "WIKI|WIKI.SPK|WikiSim|The encyclopedia: hundreds of articles from Wikipedia, as of 1996.", "ELIZA|BOT.SPK|ELIZA-95|A chatbot with Language-Model-of-Certain-Size manners.", "PAL|PAL.SPK|SimPal|Send and request money in SimBucks.", "TUBE|TUBE.SPK|SimTube|Movies: watch them, put yours up, give them stars.", "STATS|STATS.SPK|SimStats|Web statistics for any site.", "VAPOR|CATALOG.TXT|Vapor|The store: games and every SIM95 program, for your own machine."]
    IF NOT FS.Exists("C:\WEB") THEN RETURN out
    FOR EACH f IN FS.List("C:\WEB")
        IF NOT f.EndsWith("\") THEN CONTINUE
        f = f.Substring(0, f.Length - 1).Upper()
        IF FS.Exists("C:\WEB\" + f + "\APP.INF") THEN
            p = FS.Read("C:\WEB\" + f + "\APP.INF").Trim().Split("|")
            IF p.Count >= 2 THEN
                out.Add(p[0] + "|http://" + here + "/" + f.Lower() + "/|" + p[1])
                CONTINUE
            END IF
        END IF
        FOR EACH k IN known
            p = k.Split("|")
            IF p[0] = f AND FS.Exists("C:\WEB\" + f + "\" + p[1]) THEN out.Add(p[2] + "|http://" + here + "/" + f.Lower() + "/|" + p[3])
        NEXT
    NEXT
    RETURN out
END FUNCTION
